# Ghostty configuration.
#
# Lives at the XDG path rather than
# ~/Library/Application Support/com.mitchellh.ghostty/config.ghostty because
# Ghostty reads both on macOS and only this one on Linux. Note it MERGES the
# two when both exist, so keep only this one.
#
# TERMINAL APPEARANCE ONLY. The shell itself — prompt, history, aliases,
# completion, secrets — is global: every terminal and SSH session reads
# ~/.zshrc and ~/.zprofile. Nothing shell-related is set here, so there is
# exactly one obvious place to change the shell: the dotfiles repo's dot_zshrc.
#
# The theme names and the light/dark mode are not set here at all: they come
# from .chezmoidata/palette.toml (three settings -- browse the names with
# `ghostty +list-themes`). theme = "system" renders the light:/dark: pair
# Ghostty auto-switches with the OS; "light"/"dark" pin one theme for the
# whole stack. The rest of the stack follows the same signal: the zsh prompt
# uses indexed colors 0-15, Neovim sets 'background' via
# lua/bruce/core/appearance.lua, and delta-theme (~/.local/bin, wired into
# git and lazygit) picks the matching syntax theme.
theme = {{ if eq .palette.theme "system" -}}
light:{{ .palette.light_theme }},dark:{{ .palette.dark_theme }}
{{- else if eq .palette.theme "light" -}}
{{ .palette.light_theme }}
{{- else -}}
{{ .palette.dark_theme }}
{{- end }}
